  "body": "The stable NAS channel (`S:\\shows-app`) had never been published, so no new computer could install. `publish-shows-channel.ps1 -Channel stable` now downloads the bundle CI attached to a `desktop-\u003csha\u003e` release (latest by default, or `-Release`) instead of compiling locally; `-Channel dev` is unchanged. The launcher also failed on first run under Windows PowerShell 5.1, which its shortcut uses (`Set-Content -Encoding utf8NoBOM`), so it now writes its state file with a BOM-less UTF-8 encoder.\n\nAffected contract: `docs/feature-contracts/desktop-distribution.md`. P4 now states the stable identity is the release SHA; P1–P3 and I1–I6 are untouched, since staging, hashing and the manifest swap are the same code. Verified by publishing `fdc502c` to stable from this branch, then installing and launching on treadmill through the shortcut's 5.1 path against a copy of `shows.db`.",
  "changed_files": 5,
